#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:5
#: 4970bfb7728149fabc86cf5d76ade16a
msgid "Archived: Build Your Own Multicopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:8
#: 583f061178874faf99bb4a802277dce5
msgid "There are Lots of Ways you Can Put Together a MultiCopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:10
#: beb301dcd9e048b7b800d9b56fa2cae5
msgid "Thoughtful, slow progression is better than jumping in with both feet, you can easily get discouraged by trying to do too much too fast."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:13
#: 9ee5a49413934905a185a90117a99ddc
msgid "You are likely to have a good experience if you start with a simple, small QuadCopter, either a Ready to Fly or an All Inclusive Kit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:15
#: b61775ceba6c4ebeb6876d536d46bc15
msgid "For those with good DIY capabilities an Almost Ready To Fly build like the F450 FlameWheel described below can also work well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:17
#: 78b02db40ca34819b19ce46c9fb60b30
msgid "For your first MultiCopter, DO NOT initially try to build a Photo / Video or First Person View copter, just build a good QuadCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:19
#: 9544e71ec1774b11b009917203f36900
msgid "Even if you know that's what you really want to do, it will take you some time to come up to speed on our copters and autopilots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:21
#: 7f59a295e0884366b0e4a001582f402d
msgid "If you just want to get a taste and have a lot of fun, try one of the little inexpensive, safe, sturdy, ready to use Micro-QuadCopters below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:24
#: a4b7dfa6b7df4a729341ec1683116ac8
msgid "If you know you're serious, try the **Flamewheel ARF Build** or if you just want to fly and can afford it get the high end \\ **Iris** QuadCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:27
#: 0e1aff792d344bea9776125f30040816
msgid "The Iris includes a top end \\ **Pixhawk** autopilot and both the Iris and the Flamewheel can do **FPV** or **Video** when you are ready."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:30
#: 6c88a5fc01e1441bb7ae4144a51c14f9
msgid "Don't start with a \\ **Frame Up Build** unless you have a complete article on how to build a really good simple Quadcopter like the Flip Sport."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:33
#: 2adc3ad543284b36aaff7a0704004cae
msgid "Absolutely do not start by trying to **Build Your Own Frame**, even among experienced builders there are more failures than successes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:35
#: 923297b6e6874a63bb5605b0aced88f5
msgid "It is very important to **NOT** start out with a big (dangerous) multicopter with a bunch of photo or video stuff on it, you will regret it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:38
#: fa7b9c9509884b299b3bd6d95b0c7a97
msgid "A small, agile **QuadCopter** is always a lot more fun to fly than a big, ponderous and slow **Hex** or **OctoCopter** in any case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:40
#: 0d43403ba475498fb133f5b710580695
msgid "Except for top end professional HD video or photography requiring big cameras you are always better off thinking small, light and agile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:45
#: 0d0ccde63e7f4676ba5276887d5c98f0
msgid "Safety is very important with multicopters, keep plenty of distance from living or expensive things and review our \\ :ref:`Safety Page <safety-multicopter>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:49
#: 73242d63384041379dc8525af51ba986
msgid "Chinese Imports Good Deal / Bad Deal?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:51
#: 35e00d10f2914a7483918766d806bee2
msgid "It is very tempting especially when just starting out to buy lots of Chinese direct import stuff because it is so much cheaper: Bad Idea!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:53
#: 15cc6fbf13bb42578767a28a209b7c94
msgid "As you gain experience, you will learn which import items are serviceable, if you try to do it at the beginning things will not go well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:56
#: 05fab8ddc94a4dbfa60bbf9935bd8b9b
msgid "I recommend you always get the main electronics (autopilot) from the primary source, in our case the Pixhawk from 3DRobotics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:58
#: 8591e5eb02fb4b7086b0ef349ce2627b
msgid "You will also want to get the electronic accessories (GPS, magentometer, telemetry and OSD if used) from 3DRobotics as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:60
#: 56c009d57b4c473dba628f6359b46a85
msgid "If your going to do first person view, get a 3DRobotics FPV kit or a FatShark Attitude video goggle and transmitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:62
#: ddedacc56bda405ab3812b5286e36987
msgid "As for cameras, the GoPro Hero 3 and especially the Black is the one to get, because it is what everybody uses and it works well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:64
#: fa1e81bf1d0f401687b718c014036bc7
msgid "The DJI Flamewheel ARF kit which is recommended is made in China but is a known quality setup, so where you get it is up to you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:66
#: 8400005491894c13a6cb4f3061f9c2fa
msgid "The Traxxas, Hubsan and Helimax highly recommended starter micro-Quadcopters are also made in China but are still a great way to start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:69
#: f517a08b1c824a3e89e0afe4c1e50042
msgid "Motors, Batteries, ESCs, frames and even FRSky or Turnigy RC transmitters and receivers can be very good deals direct from China."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:71
#: ba0f9a51554946aa8eba24f08986e0be
msgid "A lot of items we buy domestically are actually made in China and of course, quality varies widely, regardless of country of origin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:73
#: f0739eb46c2045bd92a4830406b7007b
msgid "A $25.00 RC-Timer motor is not likely to be of the same quality as the equivalent $100.00 Tiger-Motor, but hey, it's only $25.00."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:75
#: b68ef6e35a9f41e19c84f97a48aad72c
msgid "Although direct Chinese imports generally have pretty reliable shipping, aftermarket support or returns are often very problematic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:77
#: 40771b8306b44f04b9a18a61f04ce216
msgid "If you build in a ten to twenty percent broken, damaged or not included expectation for Chinese imports you will not be disappointed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:80
#: a786a3a2babb4f71aa92c274873f1423
msgid "In any case, start with two or three of the recommended \"builds\" below so that you can experience success and learn to fly first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:84
#: 1a004b1411894150b2c67f3a5aacbb73
msgid "Inexpensive, Ready To Fly Nano, Micro or Small QuadCopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:88
#: 15be379d18a448beafdab78f1b27b830
msgid "If you are new to MultiCopters, I very strongly suggest you start with one of these inexpensive Ready To Fly QuadCopters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:91
#: 7e5bef58b846440da2b9a8d794a232af
msgid "They come with everything you need including the radio and the battery, require no assembly, are very sturdy and are great for learning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:94
#: e88b40d74fc84a65bf3a447dbf1097ec
msgid "They are also a ton of fun, can easily and safely be used indoors and typically cost less than a hundred dollars."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:96
#: c63ac4cd8c0846159eb67d2ece827ebf
msgid "Importantly you will get you a much better understanding of how they work and of what you really want to do next."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:98
#: a18203fc857642d1b8a32c647beb4c8f
msgid "The `Traxxas QR1 QuadCopter <http://traxxas.com/products/models/heli/6208qr1>`__ is an inexpensive RTF Micro Quadcopter that is great for a first experience. (Left image below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:101
#: 2142d8d0159f4a47845f7d1878f69e19
msgid "For $45.00 the `(Hubsan X4) <http://www.amazon.com/Hubsan-X4-H107-Copter-2-4GHZ/dp/B009M1PO7W>`__ is identical to the Traxxas and for $70.00 you can get it with a still photo and 720P HD video camera.\\ `Hubsan <http://www.amazon.com/Hubsan-X4-H107-Copter-2-4GHZ/dp/B009M1PO7W>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:106
#: 9bb370e51bc344649ed6b45cda4c0df4
msgid "For $200.00 there is even a really easy to fly **FPV** version of the `Hubsan <http://www.ebay.com/itm/like/171203630670?lpid=82\">`__ that comes with a RC transmitter with an excellent LCD display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:109
#: abfb459d2d97467b95b30ae9d49662ba
msgid "Even the parts for the Hubsans are readily available: \\ `Hobby Flip <http://hobbyflip.com/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:110
#: 68ac7c3b2e95459fa73afada96aa8f39
msgid "The \\ `Helimax 1SQ <http://www.helimax-rc.com/helicopters/hmxe0834-1sq/index.html>`__ is another low cost palm sized micro QuadCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:112
#: c39315e53b0d4792bdc7dc6763ba5f0d
msgid "Or even the really, really tiny $40.00 `Estes Proto X <http://www.amazon.com/Estes-4606-Proto-Nano-Quadcopter/dp/B00G924W98>`__ actually a Hubsan H111 which flies remarkably well (Middle and right images below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:125
#: 23899b05a27c4ca793d63d3eb81c5398
msgid "Below left is a larger, but very durable copter, the $88.00 UDI U818A 2.4GHz Quadcopter with Camera from Amazon Prime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:127
#: 686124b9fe884002bfef64c80164e140
msgid "And a link to an important `Blog Article by RocklandUSA <https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/noob-quadcopter-training-thank-you-community>`__ for all people considering their first Multicopter purchase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:129
#: d6003790fea2424f855b181519451ff7
msgid "The Blade Nano QX at $90.00 below right is also highly recommended, is very light and easy to fly and incredibly durable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:138
#: 480af502f51b41329d50ad15072d397a
msgid "If you are just starting out: Get one of these inexpensive, small, durable Quadcopters and learn to fly it well, it will save you a lot of money."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:143
#: 468b54f461ee4672949f4b937b7ad80f
msgid "All Inclusive Kit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:145
#: 40ebce899d914a51b3ff8081999ab560
msgid "#. The easiest way to build is to buy a single kit that has all the parts necessary in one box and a set of instructions for each step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:148
#: e62c5e4c25fa408095a233fbb7587ef4
msgid "#. Outside of (Ready To Fly) a good all inclusive kit is the most reliable and straightforward way to construct a quality MultiCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:151
#: 6c1fd8cdaa8049c388295a770e07409f
msgid "#. Usually all of the components are well balanced with each other and the entire craft can be expected to perform well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:154
#: e6ca02366e574495bb3f6d36a10dec4a
msgid "#. For an all inclusive kit, assembly is just nuts and bolts and possibly some soldering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:157
#: d2a874092fdd4a4dad899f1d91dfc65b
msgid "#. The assembly procedure is usually well explained in the supplied instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:160
#: da4a2cebaeeb4185ad4d38ef198461f5
msgid "#. The downside is that often quality kits are a bit more expensive than other alternatives and customization has to be added on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:163
#: 0d0305e05a564e629a6499683b15fb91
msgid "#. If you are not already well qualified at Do It Yourself projects, A good all inclusive kit is definitely the best place to start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:166
#: cdfa20b91f844edc936c039d42e24034
msgid "#. The innovative `Iris QuadCopter <https://www.amazon.com/3DRobotics-3DR0171-3DR-IRIS-Quadcopter/dp/B00NWXY076>`__ is actually \\ **Ready To Fly** and comes with the top of the line **Pixhawk** autopilot. However, these are no longer produced/sold by 3DR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:170
#: 453e1276cbc84a789141aa5d0f883d36
msgid "It is capable of fully autonomous flight and includes the RC transmitter, the battery and even telemetry, at $750.00 it is a real bargain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:173
#: eef72ae3a76940559900827147d0a90f
msgid "The Iris structurally strong and resilient and it is set up to support a GoPro camera or even FPV (First Person View) when you are ready."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:181
#: 25edba353a4f42c3a0f62c2c625ca9c1
msgid "Almost Ready to Fly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:183
#: beea647489c04a0d8197afa263a4e334
msgid "If you need everything and want the most versatile copter possible you can't beat the Iris above, it is simply a great deal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:185
#: 9e29e6cd8b024338834e41d99ad967e3
msgid "If you already have a RC transmitter you can save some money and still build a really high quality autonomous QuadCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:187
#: ef23ef6bed2e4dbdb7eba01d9f6f6f71
msgid "Even if you are just starting there are a few really good choices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:189
#: e5255a7010854ade89da593180bbf1a1
msgid "The **DJI F450 Flamewheel QuadCopter ARF Kit** may well be single the best choice at this time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:191
#: 2d591b4e27ee435ca70d507c1e6a8585
msgid "This kit comes with frame with built in power distribution board, the 4 motors and the 4 Electronic Speed Controls and 8 Propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:193
#: 051682eea8c242a1a8ac464481d29990
msgid "You need to add a :ref:`Pixhawk <common-pixhawk-overview>` Flight controller, A battery and your Radio Control Transmitter and Receiver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:196
#: 90302ef65c954c568c58dfe3bea22487
msgid "The supplied equipment in the kit is all first rate and the real DJI Flamewheel frame is very stiff and sturdy (a good thing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:198
#: e9ba87b035964518aaac9a90369cd4c7
msgid "Cost: F450 ARF kit $180.00, Pixhawk with GPS/Compass $280.00 and a Battery $35.00 = ($495.00) plus a PPM-Sum receiver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:201
#: e0cc56d006944208879e29c204d3c330
msgid "As an alternative, the smaller **DJI F330 Flamewheel Quadcopter** is also an excellent choice and can be better in smaller spaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:204
#: 956f249176684ca49c04f19078978f2d
msgid "The :ref:`Wiki page on constructing the F330 <dji-f330-flamewheel>` is applicable to the **F450** as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:207
#: 516030f61726428d8bf691aa67faaaa8
msgid "Most ARF kits that are cheaper than this are not nearly as sturdy and the components generally fail much more frequently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:209
#: 1d83b1d8308d43f0acb774cd76d529f1
msgid "You can buy the `F450 ARF kit Here! <http://www.amainhobbies.com/product_info.php/cPath/2_382_2405_3233_3237/products_id/235232/n/DJI-Innovations-Flame-Wheel-F450-ARF-Quadcopter-Kit-w-Motors-ESC-Propellers>`__ This source has the **F350 ARF** kit also."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:211
#: 108a8050ad9f49099022720c1c97faab
msgid "DO NOT get a clone kit that looks like it, the real DJI motors and ESCs are top quality and the frame is stiff and strong, the clones are not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:214
#: e7f8ea9a6e754e8f952a69d1d1417ca1
msgid "There are more expensive high quality ARF kits available but the FlameWheels will give great service and have very high performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:216
#: f215dfd470f94eef89eb2c07b03afbd7
msgid "If you want to keep initial cost to a bare minimum, start with a `Simple Flight Controller <http://www.hobbyking.com/hobbyking/store/__24723__Hobbyking_KK2_0_Multi_rotor_LCD_Flight_Control_Board.html>`__ then graduate to a `Pixhawk <https://store.3dr.com/products/3dr-pixhawk>`__ when you are ready"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:221
#: 87aa41bd6d894e3ab143580db904fc84
msgid "The F450 can also serve as a competent Gopro and Gimbal carrying photo and video copter or as an FPV platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:223
#: 137a9aabee1f4b03a8023fbf756ac4a7
msgid "The **DJI F550 ARF Hexacopter** is a good choice for more advanced uses, but it is not ideal as a first MultiCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:230
#: 6883b4bb3de84b36842918d15cfb1efe
msgid "Frame Kit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:232
#: d69562580d9e48ec90d3b31a52132eb2
msgid "Once you get into building your own MultiCopter based on a frame kit you are getting into the big leagues, this is really not for beginners."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:235
#: e3260449dca34067aca4ccf9411118cf
msgid "The exception is if you are carefully following a specific and highly detailed build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:237
#: 300b849b8d114bc8a2485140d03d965d
msgid "I am working on 2 Frame Kit based builds at the moment, a Flip 380 Sport QuadCopter and a Tarot 650 Carbon Fiber Quadcopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:239
#: d190229b37454573a12ee42071bd2810
msgid "A little bit on the reasons for and methods used in each of the Builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:241
#: b0fe58213a2743eaa2e7239212c382f1
msgid "The Hoverthings \\ `Flip 380 Sport <http://www.hoverthings.com/the-flip-black>`__ Frame is billed as the most indestructible frame ever."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:244
#: 1f0ce98774a9474d8c3fc58f6861332e
msgid "It uses incredibly stiff and strong CNC machined 1/4\" thick Fiberglass arms and G10 Fiberglass center plates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:246
#: fc6cdbc6cef64c69a6beb9aed37cd349
msgid "It can incorporate the same motors and ESCs as used in the DJI Flamewheel and can use up to 10\" propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:248
#: 818df0ad78f84e5582abddf7adca32c8
msgid "I purchased the Flip Sport Kit plus an extra pair of \"tab\" type center sections and extra 7/8\" spacers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:250
#: 13e61a67c1354f9cb5006967c613d4d2
msgid "The extra center plates mount below the stock plates on 7/8\" spacers to accommodate the battery and flight gear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:252
#: 33097ddc5c8f4e2caff2ec4b26fd4b39
msgid "I am using 4 of the stock DJI Flamewheel motors and a special `4 in 1 ESC <http://mymobilemms.com/OFFTHEGRIDWATER.CA/index.php?main_page=product_info&cPath=2_4&products_id=203>`__ placed between the center plates of the copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:258
#: 9a39d5e73b82463c9eb1d4b165184bac
msgid "The 4 in 1 ESC produces much less RF and DC interference and is neater than 4 ESCs and a power distribution board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:260
#: c3b6aef87c6d4735b6683100237756c9
msgid "I am using `GemFan DJI hub compatible 10\" carbon filled propellers <http://www.rcdude.com/servlet/the-2498/GemFan-DJI-Hub-10x4.5/Detail>`__ because they are very tough and very efficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:262
#: 799afe67e5a949feb56e7ab10bd5da79
msgid "My goal is to build an even tougher and higher performance copter than the DJI F450 Flamewheel - inexpensively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:264
#: 85261197a0424aa597427e262cbeeb7b
msgid "Although it's a small copter the Flip is powerful and agile enough to use FPV video and/or a GoPro Camera and brushless gimbal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:266
#: 2683f356e5d3420792d9057007012f45
msgid "Here is a link to the :ref:`Hoverthings Flip Sport Quadcopter Wiki Build Page <hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter>` using a Pixhawk autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:271
#: 29729a1150464cc9b0e0fbaa252f98cf
msgid "The `Tarot 650 <http://www.ebay.com/itm/Tarot-Iron-Man-650-Foldable-3K-carbon-fiber-Quad-copter-Quadcopter-Frame-TL65B02-/151050276421>`__ is a carbon fiber frame that is quite large for a QuadCopter and it can incorporate up to 17\" propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:275
#: 49f9be4ce3b34590bacecfebd8ac5728
msgid "I am using 360kv slow speed, large diameter \\ **Pancake Motors** designed to turn the more efficient large propellers at low speeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:278
#: c13f84a50e8f4c00af0dac5f6d4c0263
msgid "I will be using a variety of 14\" to 17\" propellers to explore performance and efficiency at various propeller diameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:280
#: 47e89fae751542079c271663c8c3b65a
msgid "Although the Flip Sport build shown above could be appropriate for a first QuadCopter, this Tarot 650 build is definitely not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:282
#: f982a8b7419f4255846283b979775837
msgid "This quad is big enough to serve as a heavy lift or long endurance copter or to carry a big video or still camera, but:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:285
#: d3c215d4f52e486c9056a985e441524e
msgid "For lifting a 2KG payload with a quadcopter you need some serious motor and some serious prop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:287
#: 1d40952b12fd46fc85d7757bb2315369
msgid "`Four Tigermotor MN4010 475 KV motors <http://www.rctigermotor.com/html/2013/Navigator_0910/38.html>`__ at $86.00 each, four 15 x 5 or 16 x 5 props and four high quality 30 amp ESCs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:290
#: 3005988a48254fc5a25a9480940af8d0
msgid "It needs 10,000mah of 4 cell Lipo batteries (two 5000's) to achieve approximately ~10 minutes of flight time at 4KG total weight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:293
#: 0cdf1ccc03ba4da4a87b6b55fb9705aa
msgid "It should be capable of lifting 4 KG total (including 2KG payload) and leave about 50% reserve thrust (minimum needed) (6kg total)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:296
#: f0a7a753a75149f3917cd83e4e80c7a7
msgid "You will need 16\" x 5  props to achieve the thrust and efficiency necessary to lift 4KG total with reasonable flight times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:299
#: 0377fceebf0b47ee884a65d463b50e13
msgid "That is why the bigger motors with the lower KV are required and they need to be high quality to withstand continuous high output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:302
#: 1e23ac8c535445029175a08453146634
msgid "It is very highly recommended that you do not attempt to construct one of these for your first build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:305
#: d3bf161e8fdb4c98ad6d9e4c55d99009
msgid "A really handy link for quickly calculating performance requirements for various multicopters and components: `eCalc <http://www.ecalc.ch/indexcalc.htm>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:312
#: f132d1699f174a0e80df83766fc545f9
msgid "**Or Perhaps a really tiny little `250 sized $10.00 frame <http://www.hobbyking.com/hobbyking/store/__47075__HobbyKing_FPV250_Quad_Copter_A_Mini_Sized_FPV_Multi_Rotor_kit_.html>`__ with FPV capability you can fly indoors or out.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:322
#: 2d1c959905544828ad92a0e88d190d18
msgid "Scratch Built"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:324
#: fe4a9482a876414eae20c60aa97074f2
msgid "Although this is often attempted by those who have never used a multicopter, it very seldom turns out well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:326
#: 526ac3ce6f244418bbe7621b3dc3a79b
msgid "At the simplest level a functioning QuadCopter can be built out of sticks or dowels and plywood that will fly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:328
#: 0cfab86fa34a49e7b379ecb042ba84c9
msgid "But it is very unlikely to fly well or to be very serviceable or to well tolerate less than perfect \"landings\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:330
#: 246464aea8bb44b8b63b83a337734d92
msgid "And this is no way to save money, RTF, Kits and ARF include high quality matched components and actually cost less."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:332
#: 026127fcc58347438206300c44e9084a
msgid "Even if you are an experienced model builder, machinist or engineer, DO NOT START HERE!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:334
#: e7077ac06efe4144930f4bdc52f1b676
msgid "Multicopters have their whole own set of flight dynamics and structural demands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:336
#: b3a0321507e34cdcb62794e2224074a4
msgid "Until you have become experienced with them you stand virtually no chance of designing and making a worthwhile MultiCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:338
#: d4408cf6153a46e2a0e510958c9ad3ba
msgid "There is a really lovely QuadCopter design made by a newbie from bent sheet aluminum on our site right now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:340
#: a77423d80fad4beba8db8a5cb425aa94
msgid "Unfortunately sheet aluminum is soft, the copter is heavy and hard landings are common so a very bent copter is inevitable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:342
#: cfbf8dfe894b440a83064b9afba2547d
msgid "Even if you are very experienced, you will certainly need to make several copters before you achieve a worthwhile design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:344
#: b9cd407def8e4752b0beff41c13cd071
msgid "I won't say Experts only, but you really need to go through at least 3 or 4 commercial MultiCopters before you even think about doing this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:347
#: 8c7d922d7cdb4852864bc28b66c5232f
msgid "I have made over a dozen different CAD designs so far and have not yet built one, I will make one, but I'm not ready yet and I know it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:351
#: bf92c5d9082d445d93eeb526e5a9aacd
msgid "Brand Name Ready to Fly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:353
#: d767d10f426842a48d23d1c9816763eb
msgid "A few words about the **Brand Name** Ready To Fly QuadCopters like the **Parrot**, the **DJI Phantom** and the **Blade 350QX**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:356
#: f086303371e04a02bb585f40f3aae78d
msgid "Within the scope of their capabilities these are generally well made and often a reasonable bargain for what they do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:358
#: 42e74c8bf5e44406b91d996f66db9c8c
msgid "But they are also not easily modified or improved on and are not easy to upgrade to a more powerful autopilot like the Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:360
#: 2d53bed6c22a4b64819120dd6a8f6c3b
msgid "So although they are a moderately capable one stop solution, they can also be a bit of a costly dead end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:362
#: bc14cc5da1da40ad8ddd8c3b16478c56
msgid "You can put together a **Flamewheel ARF kit** with a top end **Pixhawk autopilot** for about the same money and be way ahead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:367
#: a49f1371a47c4910adcb63f167527bb0
msgid "Which Approach is Right for You"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:369
#: 65dae2092d5048b295f038f2b776caf0
msgid "It is very important to match your approach to your capability level, if you overreach you can end up with a negative experience."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:371
#: 6d7a721c72e44c5ca7a5530e6bf10f52
msgid "It is also much more important to take a robust and conservative approach than to try to do everything the first time out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:374
#: 40ffdc6fbbff429cb365bebb3cae04ed
msgid "The simplest approach is to get a **Ready to Fly** system or an **All Inclusive Kit**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:376
#: c78d54a4cf4844d88c0708e67f92b9f8
msgid "However, a good **Almost Ready To Fly** kit plus some carefully chosen components can also result in an outstanding copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:378
#: 70cb7e9abb8347019a469de3450080f6
msgid "The ARF approach can often cost somewhat less and enable you to construct a copter that is specifically tailored to your needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:380
#: 621ea53891e04d0881dcefffb8712aa9
msgid "The **Frame Kit** approach presumes that you have sufficient knowledge to specify appropriate components that will work together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:383
#: 1b408d3e7dbf48738346b01766386708
msgid "But it does let you put together a copter that is specifically optimized for your needs and desires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:385
#: 4c6207c33eaa4417a347c209c79121e7
msgid "Unless you find and scrupulously follow a comprehensive article detailing a specific \"build\" a Frame Kit should not be your first copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:388
#: 675b519b37ae4d62a4a7d23371a6e514
msgid "Clearly that goes double for **Scratch Built**. It isn't actually all that hard to build a MultiCopter frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:390
#: d8be5e21d4b34283a10b6fd6a61793aa
msgid "But the overall process and component matching to make it work well is really for the experienced MultiCopter operator / builder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:393
#: 044183ccc98a4bc983828d8a7265970b
msgid "There are expensive, high end Multicopters, which are generally oriented to commercial photo or video use and outside our scope here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:395
#: 210c50f48a43453a83a26989200ba203
msgid "All of the Copters I have and will be putting together incorporate a :ref:`Pixhawk <common-pixhawk-overview>` autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:398
#: 41da3ed0dfae453295f6c31edaafef3a
msgid "These are the best and most capable autopilots available and they have great **DIYDrones** community support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:400
#: 5e770de2ea534e20a66587d5da119c9e
msgid "Beware of clones and counterfeits, they often have small differences that end up making them completely unusable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:402
#: 04ffcc1830904e269cdf1ca3ad8cd1e5
msgid "Don't say I didn't warn you: \"Caveat Emptor\" and \"You get what you pay for\"."
msgstr ""
